---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About | Arun Annavaram">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">About</h1>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      I'm Arun, a Level 3 Application Support Engineer with 7.5+ years in IT.
      My work sits where production support, identity and access, and platform
      administration meet, and I'm deliberately growing it toward SRE and DevOps.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">What I do professionally</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      <li>Investigate application issues, production incidents and Level 3 escalations, and coordinate with other teams to find root causes.</li>
      <li>Administer Jira Cloud: user management, permission schemes, project settings, governance and compliance.</li>
      <li>Handle user access requests, provisioning and deactivation.</li>
      <li>Work within access request and approval workflows (SailPoint) and group synchronization with Active Directory.</li>
      <li>Help keep operational processes aligned with governance and compliance requirements.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">How I think</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      I don't see my role as simply resolving tickets. I try to understand why a
      problem happened, identify its underlying cause, and look for ways to
      prevent it from happening again, often by automating something repetitive.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">What I'm learning</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      Separate from my day job, these are skills I'm building independently. I'm
      not claiming production experience in them yet.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      <li>Linux</li>
      <li>Python scripting for DevOps automation</li>
      <li>Jira APIs, exploring integration and automation possibilities</li>
      <li>Docker, Kubernetes and cloud fundamentals</li>
    </ul>
  </main>
</Layout>